From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:26:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 537/537] [DS4.1] MXFP8 GEMMs load the 32x32 block-scale grid
 at SFB[row // 32]

The block-32 FP8 projections packed their UE8M0 block scales once per output
row (pack_scale_words(..., rows=N)): the 32x32 grid repeated 32 times, so a
decode step read 32 copies of every scale word beside the weight. The GEMMs
now take the grid itself and load SFB[row // 32]; the expanded tensor
satisfies expanded[row] == block[row // 32], so every loaded word, and so
every output bit, is the one the broadcast gave. Grouped weights are stacked
in N, so the same index serves them; WO-A's raw exponent grid is read the
same way. _block32_scale_words refuses a scale grid whose rows are not one
per 32 outputs.

Candidate 9 measurements (one-at-a-time experiment, 2026-10-28): block-32
GEMM output digests equal over 182 cases (seven TP4 shapes, 1-16 decode rows
and prefill rows); serving determinism, greedy and sampled digests equal;
decode grid 1.3% faster, 131K prefill 1.1% faster, beyond the repeat.
